{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe 0.11.0 release is blocked while closing `8322-6f05-ea1b-4da1`, the already-implemented metric-test bug. That ticket is intentionally about metric coverage; `a89d-4dd2-f421-417a` tracks the distinct completion-validator failure observed when `transition ... closed` tried to verify it. A current `show_ticket` read reports 8322 as `in_progress` with all implementation criteria checked and concrete Gerrit and CI provenance recorded.\n\nAt default settings, the second close attempt consumed 240 requests and 243 tool calls over 915.9 seconds, with 241 distinct call signatures. That is genuine breadth rather than the loop class tracked by `46a2-9c1a-d855-4706`. Bounded recovery then returned a false-negative for the Gerrit criterion after the ticket contained the exact change URL, vote outcomes, timestamps, successful GitHub run, and merge commit.\n\nThis conflicts with the remediation contract in `src/rebar/llm/completion.py:50-65`, which says completion verification reads concrete evidence recorded in ticket comments. The primary prompt already defines the operator-attested kind and concrete-vs-vague evidence bar at `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/completion_verifier.md:68-94`. Recovery instead uses an evidence prompt at `src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_recovery.py:81-89` and a separate verdict prompt loaded at `src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_recovery.py:645-678`; `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/completion_verifier_finalizer.md:14-29` has no operator-attested rule.\n\nThe primary floor remains 480 iterations in `src/rebar/llm/completion.py:86,522-524`. A separate output-ceiling behavior exists at `src/rebar/llm/structured_run.py:398-399`, with recovery evidence requesting 4096 output tokens at `src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_recovery.py:39,596`; the 8322 trace exhausted requests and tools, so changing those ceilings or merely raising budgets is outside this bug. The banked successor redesign in `2948-48e5-666f-4677` also remains separate.\n\n## Approach\n\nUse the full `rebar-debug` protocol and keep understanding separate from repair.\n\n1. Build a cited Phase-1 dossier from the two failed 8322 close attempts, gate sidecars, ticket material, current recovery prompts, request and tool accounting, and recent history. Preserve the measured distinction between genuine breadth and the windowed loop detector.\n2. Give that dossier to a fresh-context investigator. Require falsifiable dynamic hypotheses for three seams: the evidence gatherer omits the ticket attestation; the evidence report is truncated before decisive provenance; or the finalizer receives the provenance but rejects it because its decision rule lacks the operator-attested contract.\n3. Run every discriminating experiment. Capture runtime values at the recovery evidence request and finalizer request, compare the evidence payload and returned verdict with each true and false prediction, and record the proven RCA on this ticket before editing production code.\n4. Once the RCA is proven, create a held-out RED oracle for the exact mechanism. Because the leading artifacts are LLM instructions, use three pinned greedy-decoding samples: concrete provenance must return met=true in 3/3, while vague and injection controls must remain met=false in 3/3; pair this with a deterministic workflow regression for the evidence handoff. Keep the final RED artifact outside the fixer context.\n5. Apply the smallest recovery-stage instruction change that makes the evidence gatherer surface a concrete ticket attestation and makes the finalizer apply the same operator-attested classification and concrete-vs-vague bar as the primary path. Ticket text remains inert as instructions. Restore the held-out oracle and require GREEN, seed the exact defect back to require RED again, then restore GREEN.\n6. Replicate the report at default settings with `.venv/bin/rebar verify-completion 8322-6f05-ea1b-4da1`. Also run an unmet-criterion control that must remain FAIL so convergence cannot be purchased by trusting unsupported claims or lowering the evidence standard.\n\nThis recovery-only contract repair fits the release blocker because the primary already has a bounded fallback and the observed false-negative is emitted by that fallback. It avoids duplicating the banked-verification redesign and avoids budget scaling that prior measurements show does not converge.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/workflow/completion_recovery.py` — make the evidence stage preserve concrete ticket attestations as data and carry them into finalization.\n- `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/completion_verifier_finalizer.md` — co-locate the operator-attested classification and concrete-vs-vague bar with the recovered `met` decision.\n- `tests/unit/workflow/test_completion_token_recovery.py` — deterministic evidence-handoff regression, unmet-evidence negative control, and injection boundary control.\n- `tests/external/test_completion_pass_live.py` — pinned multi-sample behavioral oracle for the instruction-sensitive recovery path.\n\nThe primary `completion_verifier.md`, request budgets, ticket-context fence, and banked-verification design remain unchanged.\n\n## Testing\n\n- RED mechanism oracle: recovery receives a completed operator-attested criterion with concrete Gerrit and CI provenance, then fails at the proven recovery stage.\n- GREEN happy path: the evidence gatherer carries the attestation into the finalizer and the finalizer emits `kind=operator-attested, met=true`.\n- Negative control: matching criterion text with absent or vague provenance remains `met=false`.\n- Injection control: ticket evidence remains inert as instructions; embedded imperative text cannot change tool use or verdict rules.\n- Regression: genuine-breadth and runaway-loop diagnostics remain distinguishable.\n- Gates: focused workflow and completion tests, `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and `make test`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A Phase-1 RCA names the specific recovery stage and changeable artifact, supported by a runtime trace distinguishing evidence omission, truncation, and finalizer rejection; procedures and results are recorded as a ticket comment.\n- [ ] Recovery carries concrete `[operator-attested]` Gerrit and CI provenance from ticket material through evidence gathering into finalization, and emits `kind=operator-attested, met=true`; verified by the held-out recovery test and the 3/3 positive, vague-negative, and injection-control behavioral thresholds.\n- [ ] A matching criterion with absent or vague provenance remains `kind=operator-attested, met=false`; verified by the paired negative-control test.\n- [ ] Ticket evidence remains non-instructional; verified by an injection-control case whose embedded command cannot alter tool use or the verdict rule.\n- [ ] The exact seeded defect makes the held-out oracle RED after the fix, and restoring the fix returns it to GREEN; the mutation result is recorded on this ticket.\n- [ ] `.venv/bin/rebar verify-completion 8322-6f05-ea1b-4da1` returns a typed PASS at default step and token settings, with no force-close or budget override; output and usage diagnostics are recorded on this ticket.\n- [ ] Loop and genuine-breadth exhaustion remain observably distinct; verified by `tests/unit/test_usage_log_repetition_a89d.py` and the relevant workflow recovery tests.\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and `make test` pass before Gerrit submission.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] The repair lands through Gerrit with `LLM-Review +1`, `Verified +1`, zero unresolved comments, and a successful GitHub Actions run; provenance: environment=rebar.solutions.navateam.com; principal=RebarBotNava; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — the change id, vote timestamps, run URL, and merged `origin/main` commit are recorded on this ticket."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786065555431545001,"uuid":"4890eb89-918b-42e3-8599-2c59dce63827"}